    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 9th with a clear emphasis on exploiting speed and platoon advantages. Our strongest play is **Trea Turner** (76.84), who benefits from a prime leadoff spot against the southpaw Freeland, buoyed by a strong historical BvP and park factors that make him the pivot point of today\u2019s offensive strategy. Not far behind is **Kyle Schwarber** (72.30), whose platoon advantage against the same left-handed arm keeps his value high, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.16), whose aggressive jump-rate against the slow delivery of Leiter makes him a priority start in our pursuit of scarce stolen bases. Despite facing the high-velocity Strider, **Hyeseong Kim** (61.54) remains in the lineup; while his order placement hurts, his efficiency against right-handed pitching keeps him locked into our 2B slot.\n\nThe decision to bench **Gary Sanchez** was the most straightforward of the morning, as his lack of a confirmed lineup spot and unfavorable park/pitcher skill metrics relegated him to the pine, while the rainouts of **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin** simplified our roster construction significantly. We are keeping a close eye on **Yordan Alvarez** (58.52); although he is an elite talent, the matchup against the formidable Burns is our most significant risk of the day, forcing a score drop despite his high-end xwOBA. Elsewhere, **Colt Keith** (64.94), **Carson Benge** (64.10), and **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.54) provide reliable, high-floor output in their respective slots. We will monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** on the IL and ensure that depth pieces like **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** remain ready should our dynamic lineup require late-game adjustments.",
